### T05 — Karaoke word-highlight captions as the transcript device
- **Timestamps:** throughout (bottom band).
- **Mechanics:** the creator's own burned-in Persian captions sit in a fixed bottom band; the currently spoken word renders in full white while the rest of the line sits dimmed, so the highlight sweeps the line in reading order, word by word, locked to the voice. The caption is the specimen's own — this packet adds no captions to any sample (production record, caption disposition).
- **Why it works:** in a faceless piece, the moving highlight is the persona's visible "speech act" — the eye is pulled to the exact word the machine is saying, which keeps a static diagram feeling spoken.
- **Evidence:** ev/066-house-scene.jpg (highlight mid-line) · ev/080-house-clock-verdict.jpg (highlight at line start) · clip clips/000-bayes-board-build.mp4 (sweep visible across lines). Form: frame + clip (sweep timing is the mechanic).

### T06 — Day-counter UI as section machinery
- **Timestamps:** counter visible ≈32–58 s and in report cards ≈91–116 s.
- **Mechanics:** a small segmented control at top centre reads روز ("Day") with three numbered cells (۱ ۲ ۳); the active day is boxed bright, the others dim. The simulation's days advance by flipping the active cell — the section structure of the whole piece is this one UI widget, reused at every day change.
- **Why it works:** a 155 s monologue gets chapters without title cards; the viewer always knows which day of the experiment they are in, and the "report" framing stays alive.
- **Evidence:** ev/034-day1-ui-build.jpg (day 1 active, figures assembling) · ev/050-day2-resource-bars.jpg (counter over day-2 scene). Form: frame; the flip itself is a beat inside clip clips/100-chart-plunge.mp4's wider window class — ruled stills-sufficient for the counter (the claim is the state system, not the flip's easing; easing UNRESOLVED).

### T07 — Resource bars over standing figures (day-2 depletion scene)
- **Timestamps:** ≈49–58 s.
- **Mechanics:** three figures stand in a row; above each, a tall thin bar outline (labels paraphrased — small text: fresh money / waiting relationships / a die icon) stands nearly empty, with a small filled segment at the base of the middle bar. Below, an empty rounded report panel waits. The bars do not animate down on screen — depletion is shown as an already-low state, held.
